  "summary_en": "Florida's Unmanned Aircraft Systems Act (s. 330.41) vests drone regulation in the state, preempts local ordinances, protects drone delivery ports from local denial, and criminalizes drone operation or contact over critical infrastructure, schools, agricultural lands, and private property, with exemptions and federal FAA alignment.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "State preempts local regulation of unmanned aircraft design, operation, licensing and certification.",
   "Localities cannot block drone delivery services based on drone port location.",
   "Operating drones over critical infrastructure is a third-degree felony.",
   "Drone operation over schools and agricultural lands is a misdemeanor, escalating for repeat offenses or video recording.",
   "Construed in accordance with federal statutes and FAA guidance."
